# Checkout must not rewrite bytes. The Windows CI runner (and any clone with
# core.autocrlf=true) converts LF to CRLF at checkout time, which corrupts the
# checked-in corpus fixtures *before Python ever runs*: the shipped
# `retail-close` example and the schema fixtures are compared byte-for-byte
# against regenerated trees, so a CRLF introduced by git — not by any writer
# this repo controls — fails byte-identity with no code at fault. `eol=lf`
# overrides core.autocrlf on checkout for everything git already classifies
# as text; binary files are untouched by definition of `text=auto`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit pins for the formats that carry the byte-identity claim, so they
# stay LF even if git's content heuristic ever misjudges one (an empty or
# oddly-encoded fixture can be sniffed as binary, and a later commit adding
# real content would then flip its classification mid-history):
#
# Corpus ledgers and headers — every JSONL/JSON fixture is diffed
# byte-for-byte against a regenerated corpus, so a checkout-time CRLF is a
# guaranteed false failure.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
# Prose and docs — the generated command reference under .claude/skills is
# compared verbatim by `worldloom docs --check`; CRLF on checkout would
# report it stale on every Windows machine.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.mdx   text eol=lf
# Source and config — not byte-compared, but mixed line endings churn diffs
# and Windows Python happily executes either, so nothing is gained by
# letting them float.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
# SVG is XML, i.e. text — it gets LF like any other text file. Only true
# binary formats below are exempt.
*.svg   text eol=lf

# Binary render outputs. None are tracked today, but the renderers produce
# all of these and a future golden fixture must never be line-ending
# converted: a single rewritten byte corrupts a zip container (xlsx/docx/pptx
# are zips) or a PDF xref table.
*.png  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
